---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How does authkestra-mcp secure AI agents and Model Context Protocol servers?',
    a: 'authkestra-mcp provides a 3-tier security architecture for MCP JSON-RPC tools: Tier 1 (Public) for unauthenticated read-only queries; Tier 2 (Scoped) requiring OAuth 2.1 bearer or sender-bound DPoP tokens; and Tier 3 (HumanApproved) requiring cryptographic step-up approval. Additionally, the DownstreamTokenBroker resolves third-party API credentials on the server without exposing refresh tokens or secrets in the LLM context window.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does Authkestra prevent AI agents from tampering with approved tool parameters?',
    a: 'When a tool requires Human-in-the-Loop step-up approval, Authkestra applies RFC 8785 JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS) to the tool arguments and computes a deterministic SHA-256 challenge digest over (session_id, tool_name, jcs_arguments, expires_at). If an AI agent or prompt injection alters even a single parameter value before execution, the cryptographic digest check fails and aborts the call.',
  },
  {
    q: 'When should I choose an embedded engine like Authkestra vs. Keycloak, Ory, or Zitadel?',
    a: 'Choose Authkestra when you are building Rust services or MCP servers and want in-process OAuth 2.1, Passkeys, Cedar policy, and agent tool guards with zero network hops or extra sidecar clusters. Choose a standalone IdP (Keycloak, Zitadel, Ory) if you need a turnkey admin GUI for non-technical operators, legacy SAML 2.0 federation, or a central workforce SSO portal across many non-Rust languages—you can also connect Authkestra to them via OIDC discovery.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is Re-Proof Gating and how does it prevent session escalation?',
    a: 'In many applications, an attacker who steals an active session cookie can register a new passkey or TOTP authenticator to lock out the legitimate account owner. Authkestra enforces Re-Proof Gating: enrolling high-stakes authenticators requires proving an existing primary factor (ReproofRequirement::FreshPasskey or FreshPassword) within a bounded time window.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does Stateless OAuth work without storing sessions in a database?',
    a: 'Authkestra encapsulates OAuth2 authorization state and PKCE code verifiers inside AES-256-GCM encrypted, authenticated cookies (__Host-authkestra_state). The browser holds the encrypted state during the OAuth redirect flow, and upon callback the engine verifies the authentication tag and decrypts the state in memory—scaling horizontally without a shared Redis or SQL session store.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do AI coding assistants discover Authkestra APIs via llms.txt and Agent Skills?',
    a: 'Authkestra publishes machine-readable API summaries at https://authkestra.com/llms.txt and full documentation at https://docs.authkestra.com/llms-full.txt. The official Authkestra/skills repository also provides structured Claude Code and agent skills that teach coding assistants exact typestate builder rules, Cargo feature flags, and storage traits.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I use Authkestra with any database or web framework?',
    a: 'Yes. The engine core is pure Rust with zero framework dependencies. First-party adapters are provided for Axum (authkestra-axum) and Actix-web (authkestra-actix). Persistence is defined via traits (KvStore, SessionStore, CredentialStore, OpStore) with built-in in-memory, Redis, and SQL (PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite) implementations.',
  },
];
---
<section id="faq" class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="faq-layout">
      <div class="header">
        <span class="eyebrow">ARCHITECTURE &amp; OPERATIONS</span>
        <h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Direct answers to architectural, cryptographic, and operational questions about
          Authkestra and MCP agent security.
        </p>
        <div class="faq-links">
          <a href="https://docs.authkestra.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span>Read Full Documentation</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/Authkestra/authkestra/blob/main/SECURITY.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span>Security Policy &amp; Disclosure</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
          <a href="https://play.authkestra.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span>Try Interactive Playground</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqs.map((item, idx) => (
          <details class="faq-item" open={idx === 0}>
            <summary class="faq-summary">
              <h3>{item.q}</h3>
              <div class="chevron-wrap">
                <Icon name="chevron-down" size={18} class="chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
              </div>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>{item.a}</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    max-width: var(--ak-layout-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--ak-space-24) var(--ak-space-6);
  }

  .inner {
    position: relative;
  }

  .faq-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.4fr) minmax(0, 0.6fr);
    gap: var(--ak-space-12);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .header {
    position: sticky;
    top: 6rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--ak-text-xs);
    font-family: var(--ak-font-mono);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
    letter-spacing: var(--ak-tracking-wide);
    margin-bottom: var(--ak-space-3);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-3xl);
    letter-spacing: var(--ak-tracking-tight);
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
  }

  .lead {
    margin-top: var(--ak-space-4);
    font-size: var(--ak-text-lg);
    line-height: var(--ak-leading-relaxed);
    color: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-300));
  }

  .faq-links {
    margin-top: var(--ak-space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--ak-space-3);
    padding-top: var(--ak-space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));
  }

  .faq-links a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--ak-space-2);
    font-size: var(--ak-text-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .faq-links a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .faq-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--ak-space-4);
  }

  .faq-item {
    background: hsl(var(--card));
    border: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color var(--ak-duration-fast) var(--ak-ease-out);
  }

  .faq-item:hover {
    border-color: hsl(var(--input));
  }

  .faq-item[open] {
    border-color: hsl(var(--input));
  }

  .faq-summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--ak-space-4);
    padding: var(--ak-space-5) var(--ak-space-6);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .faq-summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-summary h3 {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
    margin: 0;
    line-height: var(--ak-leading-snug);
  }

  .chevron-wrap {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: var(--ak-radius-sm);
    background: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-800));
    color: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-300));
    transition: transform var(--ak-duration-fast) var(--ak-ease-out), color var(--ak-duration-fast) var(--ak-ease-out);
  }

  .faq-summary:hover .chevron-wrap {
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
  }

  .faq-item[open] .chevron-wrap {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 var(--ak-space-6) var(--ak-space-6);
  }

  .faq-answer p {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-sm);
    line-height: var(--ak-leading-relaxed);
    color: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-300));
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .faq-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--ak-space-8);
    }
    .header {
      position: static;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .faq {
      padding: var(--ak-space-16) var(--ak-space-4);
    }
    .faq-summary {
      padding: var(--ak-space-4);
    }
    .faq-answer {
      padding: 0 var(--ak-space-4) var(--ak-space-4);
    }
  }
</style>
